      "prefLabel": "Pest range expansion",
      "altLabel": ["pest range shift", "vector expansion"],
      "definition": "Form of pest pressure characterised by the geographic spread of pests or vectors into areas that climate change has rendered newly suitable, exposing previously unaffected crops, livestock, and ecosystems.",
      "source": "IPCC AR6 WGII Ch.2: Species range shifts",
