      "prefLabel": "Abiotic hazard",
      "altLabel": ["abiotic stress", "abiotic stressor", "abiotic constraint"],
      "definition": "Climate hazard arising from non-living physical and chemical conditions of the atmosphere, water, land, and ocean, including temperature extremes, drought, flooding, storms, and soil degradation processes that harm agricultural and ecological systems.",
      "source": "IPCC AR6 WGII Ch.2",
